Shared headers, kept identical to app/src/main/cpp/gladiorenderer/include (build-guest.sh checks it):
- upload sizes honour GL_UNPACK_ALIGNMENT/ROW_LENGTH/SKIP_* (computePixelStoreDataSize), so the
  guest sends exactly the bytes the host's GLES driver reads (OpenTTD's 4-byte aligned R8 sprites
  lost their last rows before)
- pixel store state for unpack alignment/skips and the pack state in GLClientState
- 4-byte packed vertex formats (2_10_10_10, 10F_11F_11F) and GL_FIXED have a size
- depth/stencil and packed 32/64-bit pixel types have a size, GL_TEXTURE_BINDING_3D maps to 3D
- convertTexImageFormat reports when it repacked the data (host only code, the guest library
  does not change)

